# Manual seed entries (2026-06-18 13:35 CT — initial 18 entries across 3 pillars × 6 entries each)

## Pillar 1: CAC & LTV Math
2026-06-18 | #local-service | T1-Value-Bomb | Average missed HVAC call costs $400-600 in lost revenue. At 8 missed calls/day (conservative for a 1-truck shop), annualized burn is $1.0M-$1.5M. The math: 8 calls × $500/job × 320 working days/year. | Source: HVAC.com + ServiceTitan customer data 2024
2026-06-18 | #cac-ltv | T2-Authority | Lead response time: contacting a lead within 5 minutes makes you 21x more likely to qualify them vs 30 minutes. After 1 hour, the qualification rate drops to 7x. After 24 hours, 1x. | Source: Lead Response Management Study (InsideSales, Oldroyd 2011, replicated 2024)
2026-06-18 | #local-service | T1-Value-Bomb | The true cost of a missed inbound call in HVAC is $450. The LTV lost is $4,500 over 5 years. The 10x gap is why "missed call" is the single highest-leverage fix a 1-3 truck shop can make. | Source: HVAC industry benchmarks + ServiceTitan ROI calculator
2026-06-18 | #agency-ops | T2-Authority | Agency client churn averages 5-7% monthly. At 6% monthly churn, the entire client base turns over in ~17 months. The "we lost 2 clients last quarter" is not noise — it's the rate. | Source: Agency Mavericks industry survey 2024 + HubSpot agency benchmark report
2026-06-18 | #local-service | T2-Authority | Dental practice: 1 missed patient (cancellation, no-show, or unreturned call) costs $1,200-2,400 in lifetime value over 5-7 years. The "small" patient leak is the practice killer. | Source: American Dental Association + dental practice management benchmarks
2026-06-18 | #cac-ltv | T1-Value-Bomb | eCom LTV:CAC ratio: 1:3 is the bare minimum to survive, 1:5 is healthy, 1:7+ is over-investing in retention vs acquisition. Most SMB eCom shops operate at 1:1.5-2.0 and don't realize the unit economics don't work. | Source: SaaStr + Recurly + Stripe eCommerce benchmarks 2024-2025

## Pillar 2: Operational Bottlenecks
2026-06-18 | #ops-bottleneck | T2-Authority | Replacing dispatchers with AI isn't about saving a $40k salary; it's about 0-second response times during weekend surge hours. The labor cost is the wrong unit — the response window is the unit that matters. | Source: Synthflow + Air AI dispatch customer case studies
2026-06-18 | #local-service | T1-Value-Bomb | 35-45% of service business calls come outside 9-5 (weeknights, weekends, holidays). The shop owner who answers these is the shop owner who wins — the 2-3 competitor shops in the area are not staffed for it. | Source: ServiceTitan after-hours call data 2024 + HVAC.com industry survey
2026-06-18 | #ops-bottleneck | T2-Authority | Booking friction: each additional step in a booking flow drops conversion ~20%. A 5-step form vs a 2-step form is a 36% conversion gap. The "we added a question to qualify leads" refactor usually costs more leads than it filters out. | Source: BookingPress + Calendly + HubSpot booking conversion studies
2026-06-18 | #bootstrap | T1-Value-Bomb | 23% of SMBs overpay on inventory due to lack of real-time sync between POS, eCom, and warehouse. The "we keep running out of the bestsellers" symptom is a 3-system integration problem, not a forecasting problem. | Source: Lightspeed + Shopify SMB retail reports 2024
2026-06-18 | #ops-bottleneck | T2-Authority | Customer support response time: 1-hour response = 60% customer satisfaction, 24-hour response = 12%. The 23-hour gap between "fast" and "slow" support is the difference between retention and churn for most SMB SaaS. | Source: Zendesk Customer Experience Trends Report 2024 + HubSpot support benchmarks
2026-06-18 | #agency-ops | T2-Authority | 30% of agency hours go to fixing old client work (legacy retainers, technical debt from past deliverables, firefighting), not new client work. The "we're always behind" symptom is usually 30% of capacity locked in legacy work. | Source: Agency Mavericks + Dubsado agency operations survey 2024

## Pillar 3: Software Stack Friction
2026-06-18 | #stack-friction | T2-Authority | Vertical SaaS lock-in costs agencies 15% of their margin through forced payment gateways, processing fees, and "premium" tier upsells that gate the features competitors offer out of the box. The "all-in-one" pitch is a margin transfer. | Source: Agency operations consultant surveys 2024-2025 + vertical SaaS pricing comparison
2026-06-18 | #bootstrap | T1-Value-Bomb | Per-seat pricing trap: 23 SaaS tools × $50/user/month × 10 users = $11,500/month just for software — before payroll, before rent, before marketing. The "we need a tool for X" reflex compounds to 8-12% of revenue for most 10-person SMBs. | Source: Blissfully SaaS spend report 2024 (archived) + Productiv SMB SaaS benchmarks
2026-06-18 | #stack-friction | T2-Authority | Average SMB uses 14 SaaS tools but actively uses 6. The other 8 are paying for shelf-ware. Consolidation to 6-8 tools (with deliberate integration) typically cuts SaaS spend 30-40% without losing capability. | Source: Productiv + Zylo SaaS sprawl reports 2024
2026-06-18 | #stack-friction | T1-Value-Bomb | Switching cost: replacing 1 SaaS tool = 40 hours of migration work (data export, import mapping, retraining, integration re-wiring). The "we'll switch next quarter" deferral compounds — most SMBs are 2-3 tools deep in switching debt they never pay down. | Source: Migrations.io + Moveworks IT switching-cost studies 2023-2024
2026-06-18 | #bootstrap | T2-Authority | Payment processing: 2.9% + $0.30 per transaction is the standard rate, but 0.5% variance across providers (Stripe, Square, Adyen, Braintree) is real money at SMB scale. $500k annual volume × 0.5% = $2,500/year for the same product. | Source: Stripe + Square + Adyen public pricing + cardflight SMB rate analysis 2025
2026-06-18 | #stack-friction | T1-Value-Bomb | Data export hostage-taking: 40% of SaaS vendors charge extra for full data export, throttle API rate limits on free/lower tiers, or make export "available" via CSV-only (no schema, no relationships). The "you own your data" claim is aspirational, not contractual. | Source: Dunbar Cybersecurity + BetterCloud vendor lock-in survey 2024

